            <ArticleTitle>A psychosocial perspective on chronic pain and depression in the elderly.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>27-36</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chronic pain and depression often coexist in elderly individuals. This paper explores, from a clinical perspective, the antecedents for depressive symptoms in older chronic pain patients. A case is made for active social work intervention with elderly patients who manifest this complex syndrome of chronic pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
